Anouk Marchal is a late 20s human female, with red hair and dark brown eyes. She's the fraternal twin of [[Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]]. Anouk usually wears practical workshop jumpsuits, as anything fancier would likely burn or get stained by one of her experiments. She has a moderately sized raiment of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]].

Anouk is the more technologically-inclined of the twins. Her portion of the [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] workshop is covered by multimeters, oscilloscopes, and other electrical accoutrement. She tends to be more outgoing than her brother.

In [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]], she maintains a contact who runs a scrapyard — one who prefers to purchase labour directly rather than through any intermediary service, and so regularly offers work to couriers and other hands willing to deal without a middleman.

That contact is [[Copperjaw]], who runs [[Org/Sableclutch Scrap/index|Sableclutch Scrap]].

She asked the Party at the [[Sin and Tonic]] to look for her brother [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] after he went missing, and gave them the address of the cabin in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]] in his own handwriting. She offered to try to open the locked journal the Party had taken from [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] while they were away.

She and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] took their own car through the side of [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]]'s drug works and fought the henchmen he used as shields, and walked out of the collapse unhurt. She went off to rebuild the rocket hammers the work had spent, and agreed to build the Party a radio tuned to the frequency [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] gave her.

She and her brother were raised in [[Geography/Fenrith/index|Fenrith]] though born in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], and speak the language of there between them. She and Anaïs were pulled out of the [[Sin and Tonic]] and the Party with them, into a white void over an arid plain where three armed groups faced each other over two bodies and a golden box. She and her brother put a finger on the Scale to favour one side, tapping a man on each of the other two to make them fire early, and watched the fight resolve. She said it is something their mistress sets them to when she cannot be everywhere, and that this one seemed as if it might be useful.
